# CHANGELOG.md collects a new entry at the top of its [Unreleased] section on
# almost every PR. With the default 3-way merge, two branches that each add an
# entry there conflict on every rebase — the same "keep both" resolution, by
# hand, each time, with a real risk of dropping an entry. The built-in `union`
# merge driver concatenates both sides instead of raising a conflict, so both
# entries are preserved automatically. No `git config` is needed — `union` is
# a built-in driver. The ordering of the two concatenated entries is not
# guaranteed; for a changelog that is acceptable (both are dated), and the
# release step is where the section is curated.
#
# Note on the built-in `union` driver: it concatenates the two sides line-wise
# with NO dedup. If both sides edit the SAME line, it keeps BOTH copies
# silently rather than raising a conflict. This is harmless for append-only
# changelog entries (each PR adds its own distinct lines), and any duplication
# is reconciled at the release-curation step where the section is hand-curated.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
